                <pb facs="0754" n="744" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg744"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00 Revolutions/38: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Howard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-09T11:00:00-04:00">September 9, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>37. My 36, September 8, 10 a.m. Government has situation well controlled.
                    Business going on normally this morning although there are still some armed
                    troops patrolling. Minister for Foreign Affairs states that the country
                    districts are quiet.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
